  "ingredients": [
    "2 heads garlic, unpeeled",
    "5 bay leaves",
    "2 (3 ounce) packages dry crab boil",
    "1 tablespoon liquid shrimp and crab boil seasoning",
    "salt and ground black pepper to taste",
    "15 red potatoes, washed",
    "3 large oranges, halved",
    "3 large lemons, halved",
    "2 large whole artichokes",
    "2 (16 ounce) packages mushrooms, cleaned",
    "0.5 pound fresh green beans, trimmed",
    "2 large onions, sliced",
    "30 pieces baby corn",
    "2 (16 ounce) packages smoked sausage, cut into 1/2 inch slices",
    "50 live crawfish, rinsed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/x5kpO1W_8hLRSnVN48HF56Snf90=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-140993-louisiana-crawfish-boil-DDMFS-4x3-step-01-54f70f89a6f34b51bc04c9f5618ceaf7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/140993/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fill a very large pot about 1/3 full with water. Add garlic, bay leaves, dry and liquid crab boil seasonings, salt, pepper, potatoes, oranges, lemons, and artichokes. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to a simmer, and cook for 20 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Wzk5fPqzBUyVikVtN2kbyMIb6Co=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-140993-louisiana-crawfish-boil-DDMFS-4x3-step-02-59cea9d77c8e45cb98bd391c60349ad0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/140993/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in mushrooms, green beans, onions, and baby corn, and continue to cook, about 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7p2g2HjdAiAYSy-shLSKu7X9NlU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-140993-louisiana-crawfish-boil-DDMFS-4x3-step-03-1-09d7f111a9f845839b9fa90492e84e54.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/140993/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in sausage; cook 5 minutes more.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/AF3Em7nDMyU17ZN3AncMXz8O1J4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-140993-louisiana-crawfish-boil-DDMFS-4x3-step-04-d35efda1edc94c38a51b7258585653cb.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/140993/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add crawfish and return the mixture to a boil, then simmer until crawfish shells turn bright red and the tails pull out easily, about 5 minutes. Test for doneness by peeling a crawfish. Be sure not to overcook, or crawfish will become tough.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uemi_irkHk3ME9576XHHCaZFwko=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-140993-louisiana-crawfish-boil-DDMFS-4x3-step-05-6a5da8871cb147249594b11ccd6faf7a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/140993/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the heat and carefully drain all liquid. Serve the crawfish boil hot, Louisiana-style, spread over a picnic table covered with newspapers.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Je0P8QkjChxd3MfxHCne5ATHv1M=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-140993-louisiana-crawfish-boil-DDMFS-4x3-8ba42b9f86c94d5a9fa79b4cff337ea0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/140993/step_06.webp"
    }
